1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:05,359
A spider's web is stronger than it looks.

2
00:00:05,359 --> 00:00:12,158
Although it is made of thin, delicate strands, the web is not easily broken.

3
00:00:12,158 --> 00:00:17,520
However, a web gets torn every day by the insects that kick around in it, and

4
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:22,960
a spider must rebuild it when it gets full of holes.

5
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:27,760
Charlotte liked to do her weaving during the late afternoon, and Fern liked to

6
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:34,319
sit nearby and watch. One afternoon she heard a most interesting conversation

7
00:00:34,319 --> 00:00:37,679
and witnessed a strange event.

8
00:00:37,679 --> 00:00:46,479
You have awfully hairy legs, Charlotte," said Wilbur, as the spider busily worked at her task.

9
00:00:46,479 --> 00:00:52,560
"My legs are hairy for a good reason," replied Charlotte. "Furthermore, each

10
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:58,560
leg of mine has seven sections: the coxa, the troanter, the femur, the

11
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:04,000
patella, the tibia, the metatarsus, and the tarsus."

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:11,679
Wilbur sat bolt upright. "You're kidding," he said. "No, I'm not either."

13
00:01:11,679 --> 00:01:16,880
"Say those names again. I didn't catch them the first time."

14
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:26,960
"Coxa, trocanter, femur, patella, tibia, metatarsus, and tarsus." "Goodness,"

15
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:32,158
said Wilbur, looking down at his own chubby legs. I don't think my legs have

16
00:01:32,158 --> 00:01:38,880
seven sections. Well, said Charlotte, you and I lead different lives. You

17
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:45,119
don't have to spin a web. That takes real leg work. I could spin a web if I

18
00:01:45,119 --> 00:01:51,760
tried, said Wilbur, boasting. I've just never tried.

19
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:55,039
Let's see you do it, said Charlotte.

20
00:01:55,039 --> 00:02:02,000
Fern chuckled softly, and her eyes grew wide with love for the pig. "Okay,"

21
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:08,399
replied Wilbur. "You coach me, and I'll spin one. It must be a lot of fun to

22
00:02:08,399 --> 00:02:16,640
spin a web. How do I start?" "Take a deep breath," said Charlotte, smiling.

23
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:19,679
Wilbur breathed deeply.

24
00:02:19,679 --> 00:02:26,000
Now climb to the highest place you can get to. Like this. Charlotte raced up to

25
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:32,560
the top of the doorway. Wilbur scrambled to the top of the manure pile.

26
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:38,800
Very good, said Charlotte. Now make an attachment with your spinterettes. Hurl

27
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:45,039
yourself into space and let out a drag line as you go down. Wilbur hesitated

28
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:50,960
for a moment, then jumped out into the air. He glanced hastily behind to see if

29
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:55,920
a piece of rope was following him to check his fall, but nothing seemed to be

30
00:02:55,920 --> 00:03:01,119
happening in his rear. And the next thing he knew, he landed with a thump.

31
00:03:01,119 --> 00:03:05,039
Oomph, he grunted.

32
00:03:05,039 --> 00:03:11,760
Charlotte laughed so hard her web began to sway. "What did I do wrong?" asked

33
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:14,560
the pig when he recovered from his bump.

34
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:21,198
"Nothing," said Charlotte. It was a nice try. I think I'll try again, said Wilbur

35
00:03:21,198 --> 00:03:26,960
cheerfully. I believe what I need is a little piece of string to hold me. The

36
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:33,198
pig walked out to his yard. You there, Templeton? He called. The rat poked his

37
00:03:33,198 --> 00:03:36,560
head out from under the trough.

38
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:41,520
"Got a little piece of string I could borrow?" asked Wilbur. "I need it to

39
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:48,960
spin a web." Yes, indeed, replied Templeton, who saved string. No trouble

40
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:52,719
at all. Anything to oblige.

41
00:03:52,719 --> 00:03:57,760
He crept down into his hole, pushed the goose egg out of the way, and returned

42
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:01,198
with an old piece of dirty white string.

43
00:04:01,198 --> 00:04:07,520
Wilbur examined it. "That's just the thing," he said. "Tie one into my tail,

44
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:10,238
will you, Templeton?"

45
00:04:10,238 --> 00:04:16,399
Wilbur crouched low with his thin, curly tail toward the rat. Templeton seized

46
00:04:16,399 --> 00:04:22,960
the string, passed it around the end of the pig's tail, and tied two half hitches.

47
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:29,198
Charlotte watched in delight. Like Fern, she was truly fond of Wilbur, whose

48
00:04:29,198 --> 00:04:34,960
smelly pen and stale food attracted the flies that she needed, and she was proud

49
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:42,238
to see that he was not a quitter and was willing to try again to spin a web.

50
00:04:42,238 --> 00:04:47,039
While the rat and the spider and the little girl watched, Wilbur climbed

51
00:04:47,039 --> 00:04:52,800
again to the top of the manure pile, full of energy and hope. "Everybody

52
00:04:52,800 --> 00:05:02,399
watch," he cried. and summoning all his strength, he threw himself into the air head first.

53
00:05:02,399 --> 00:05:08,800
The string trailed behind him, but as he had neglected to fasten the other end to

54
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:15,279
anything, it didn't really do any good, and Wilbur landed with a thud, crushed

55
00:05:15,279 --> 00:05:19,279
and hurt. Tears came to his eyes.

56
00:05:19,279 --> 00:05:27,920
Templeton grinned. Charlotte just sat quietly. After a bit, she spoke.

57
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:34,158
You can't spin a web, Wilbur. And I advise you to put the idea out of your

58
00:05:34,158 --> 00:05:41,119
mind. You lack two things needed for spinning a web. What are they? asked

59
00:05:41,119 --> 00:05:47,600
Wilbur sadly. You lack a set of spinettes, and you lack knowhow. But

60
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:50,560
cheer up. You don't need a web.

61
00:05:50,560 --> 00:05:58,800
Zuckerman supplies you with three big meals a day. Why should you worry about trapping food?

62
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:00,960
Wilbur sighed.

63
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:06,479
You're ever so much cleverer and brighter than I am, Charlotte. I guess I

64
00:06:06,479 --> 00:06:11,119
was just trying to show off. Serves me right.

65
00:06:11,119 --> 00:06:18,399
Templeton untied his string and took it back to his home. Charlotte returned to her weaving.

66
00:06:18,399 --> 00:06:24,719
You needn't feel too badly, Wilbur," she said. "Not many creatures can spin webs.

67
00:06:24,719 --> 00:06:29,119
Even men aren't as good at it as spiders, although they think they're

68
00:06:29,119 --> 00:06:32,079
pretty good, and they'll try anything."

69
00:06:32,079 --> 00:06:40,479
"Did you ever hear of the Queensboro Bridge?" Wilbur shook his head. "Is it a web?"

70
00:06:40,479 --> 00:06:45,840
"Sort of," replied Charlotte. "But do you know how long it took men to build

71
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:52,479
it?" Eight whole years. My goodness, I would have starved to death waiting that

72
00:06:52,479 --> 00:06:57,760
long. I can make a web in a single evening. What do people catch in the

73
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:01,760
Queensboro Bridge? Bugs? asked Wilbur.

74
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:07,439
No, said Charlotte. They don't catch anything. They just keep trotting back

75
00:07:07,439 --> 00:07:14,319
and forth across the bridge, thinking there is something better on the other side.

76
00:07:14,319 --> 00:07:19,439
If they'd hang head down at the top of the thing and wait quietly, maybe

77
00:07:19,439 --> 00:07:25,119
something good would come along. But no, with men it's rush, rush, rush every

78
00:07:25,119 --> 00:07:29,679
minute. I'm glad I'm a sedentary spider.

79
00:07:29,679 --> 00:07:33,840
What does sedentary mean? asked Wilbur.

80
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:40,319
Means I sit still a good part of the time and don't go wandering all over creation.

81
00:07:40,319 --> 00:07:42,960
I know a good thing when I see it, and

82
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:49,359
my web is a good thing. I stay put and wait for what comes. Gives me a chance

83
00:07:49,359 --> 00:07:52,639
to think.

84
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:58,719
Well, I'm sort of sedentary myself, I guess, said the pig. I have to hang

85
00:07:58,719 --> 00:08:01,760
around here whether I want to or not.

86
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:07,279
You know where I'd really like to be this evening? Where? In a forest,

87
00:08:07,279 --> 00:08:13,039
looking for beach nuts and truffles and delectable roots, pushing leaves aside

88
00:08:13,039 --> 00:08:18,960
with my wonderful, strong nose, searching and sniffing along the ground.

89
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:23,198
Smelling, smelling, smelling.

90
00:08:23,198 --> 00:08:30,000
"You smell just the way you are," remarked a lamb who had just walked in.

91
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:36,560
"I can smell you from here. You're the smelliest creature in the place.

92
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:42,800
Wilbur hung his head. His eyes grew wet with tears.

93
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:48,880
Charlotte noticed his embarrassment and she spoke sharply to the lamb.

94
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:57,039
"Let Wilbur alone," she said. "He has a perfect right to smell considering his surroundings.

95
00:08:57,039 --> 00:09:00,319
You're no bundle of sweet peas.

96
00:09:00,319 --> 00:09:06,399
Furthermore, you are interrupting a very pleasant conversation. What were we

97
00:09:06,399 --> 00:09:12,719
talking about, Wilbur, when we were so rudely interrupted?

98
00:09:12,719 --> 00:09:19,198
Oh, I don't remember, said Wilbur. It doesn't make any difference. Let's not

99
00:09:19,198 --> 00:09:23,920
talk anymore for a while, Charlotte. I'm getting sleepy.

100
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:29,439
You go ahead and finish fixing your web, and I'll just lie here and watch you.

101
00:09:29,439 --> 00:09:31,840
It's a lovely evening.

102
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:36,238
Wilbur stretched out on his side.

103
00:09:36,238 --> 00:09:42,079
Twilight settled over Zuckerman's barn and a feeling of peace.

104
00:09:42,079 --> 00:09:47,359
Fern knew it was almost supper time, but she couldn't bear to leave. Swallows

105
00:09:47,359 --> 00:09:52,800
passed on silent wings in and out of the doorways, bringing food to their young

106
00:09:52,800 --> 00:10:00,000
ones. From across the road, a bird sang, "Whipperwill! Whipperwill!

107
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:05,600
Lurvy sat down under an apple tree and lit his pipe. The animals sniffed the

108
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:12,000
familiar smell of strong tobacco. Wilbur heard the trill of the tree toad and the

109
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,119
occasional slamming of the kitchen door.

110
00:10:15,119 --> 00:10:20,560
All these sounds made him feel comfortable and happy, for he loved life

111
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:23,039
and loved to be a part of the world on a

112
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:28,880
summer evening. But as he lay there, he remembered what the old sheep had told

113
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:36,880
him. The thought of death came to him, and he began to tremble with fear.

114
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:43,600
"Charlotte," he said softly. "Yes, Wilbur." "I don't want to die." "Of

115
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:48,479
course you don't," said Charlotte, in a comforting voice. "I just love it here

116
00:10:48,479 --> 00:10:54,079
in the barn," said Wilbur. "I love everything about this place." Of course

117
00:10:54,079 --> 00:10:57,600
you do," said Charlotte. "We all do."

118
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:02,479
The goose appeared, followed by her seven gosslings. They thrust their

119
00:11:02,479 --> 00:11:10,119
little necks out and kept up a musical whistling like a tiny troop of pipers.

120
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:16,880
Wilbur listened to the sound with love in his heart. "Charlotte," he said.

121
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:22,238
"Yes," said the spider. Were you serious when you promised you would keep them

122
00:11:22,238 --> 00:11:28,719
from killing me? I was never more serious in my life. I am not going to

123
00:11:28,719 --> 00:11:34,319
let you die, Wilbur. How are you going to save me?" asked Wilbur, whose

124
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:39,439
curiosity was very strong on this point.

125
00:11:39,439 --> 00:11:47,520
"Well," said Charlotte vaguely, "I don't really know, but I'm working on a plan."

126
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:50,800
That's wonderful, said Wilbur.

127
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:56,319
How is the plan coming, Charlotte? Have you got very far with it? Is it coming

128
00:11:56,319 --> 00:12:02,079
along pretty well? Wilbur was trembling again. But Charlotte was cool and

129
00:12:02,079 --> 00:12:08,079
collected. Oh, it's coming all right, she said lightly. The plan is still in

130
00:12:08,079 --> 00:12:15,520
its early stages and hasn't completely shaped up yet, but I'm working on it.

131
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:18,719
When do you work on it? begged Wilbur.

132
00:12:18,719 --> 00:12:24,000
When I'm hanging head down at the top of my web. That's when I do my thinking,

133
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:29,439
because then all the blood is in my head. I'd be only too glad to help in

134
00:12:29,439 --> 00:12:34,479
any way I can. Oh, I'll work it out alone, said Charlotte. I can think

135
00:12:34,479 --> 00:12:40,319
better if I think alone. All right, said Wilbur. But don't fail to let me know if

136
00:12:40,319 --> 00:12:45,760
there's anything I can do to help, no matter how slight.

137
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:52,479
Well, replied Charlotte, you must try to build yourself up. I want you to get

138
00:12:52,479 --> 00:13:00,079
plenty of sleep and stop worrying. Never hurry and never worry. Chew your food

139
00:13:00,079 --> 00:13:04,960
thoroughly and eat every bit of it, except you must leave just enough for

140
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:08,238
Templeton. Gain weight and stay well.

141
00:13:08,238 --> 00:13:14,238
That's the way you can help. Keep fit and don't lose your nerve. Do you think

142
00:13:14,238 --> 00:13:20,639
you understand? Yes, I understand, said Wilbur.

143
00:13:20,639 --> 00:13:23,520
Go along to bed, then, said Charlotte.

144
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:29,198
Sleep is important. Wilbur trotted over to the darkest corner of his pin and

145
00:13:29,198 --> 00:13:32,880
threw himself down. He closed his eyes.

146
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:35,760
In another minute, he spoke.

147
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:42,000
Charlotte," he said. "Yes, Wilbur. May I go out to my trough and see if I left

148
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:48,800
any of my supper? I think I left just a tiny bit of mashed potato." "Very well,"

149
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:54,960
said Charlotte, "but I want you in bed again without delay."

150
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:58,000
Wilbur started to race out to his yard.

151
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:05,760
"Slowly, slowly," said Charlotte. Never hurry and never worry. Wilbur checked

152
00:14:05,760 --> 00:14:09,119
himself and crept slowly to his trough.

153
00:14:09,119 --> 00:14:14,560
He found a bit of potato, chewed it carefully, swallowed it, and walked back

154
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:21,359
to bed. He closed his eyes, and was silent for a while. "Charlotte," he said

155
00:14:21,359 --> 00:14:23,840
in a whisper, "Yes.

156
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:26,800
May I get a drink of milk? I think there

157
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:31,119
are a few drops of milk left in my trough."

158
00:14:31,119 --> 00:14:38,639
No, the trough is dry and I want you to go to sleep. No more talking. Close your

159
00:14:38,639 --> 00:14:41,520
eyes and go to sleep.

160
00:14:41,520 --> 00:14:47,840
Wilbur shut his eyes. Fern got up from her stool and started for home, her mind

161
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:52,880
full of everything she had seen and heard. Good night, Charlotte, said

162
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:58,479
Wilbur. Good night, Wilbur. There was a pause. Good night, Charlotte. Good

163
00:14:58,479 --> 00:15:04,079
night, Wilbur. Good night. Good night.

164
00:15:04,079 --> 00:15:06,639
Chapter 10.

165
00:15:06,639 --> 00:15:09,960
An explosion.
